// One step of that search: the name, if this function's node is at or after
// the node being placed, and "" (keep looking) otherwise.

fn_covers(int i, int id) {
  string s = "";
  if((import prog)[i] >= id) {
    s = s1_of((import prog)[i]);
  }
} return string s;

// The line to report. The parser fills nline for statement nodes, which is
// where idc.py reports all but three of these diagnostics, so those land on
// exactly the same line. An expression node has no line of its own and falls
// back to its function's -- the same compromise the structural checks make.
tc_line(int id) {
  int n = (import nline)[id];
  if(n == 0) {
    n = func_line(node_fn(id));
  }
} return int n;
